# Intent: The pure core of the passcode lock (maipai_lock_core.h, plain C99, host tested): the lock state, a salted and stretched hash of a 4 to 6 digit code (PBKDF2 with HMAC-SHA-256, 2000 rounds, a 16 byte random salt the caller supplies; the code itself is never stored), set, change and clear (a change or a clear needs the current code and neither works while locked), lock now, the auto lock timer (off, 1, 5, 15, 30 or 60 idle minutes; a ringing alarm or timer and a turn in progress hold it off), the keypad rules (a 3 by 4 grid of 44 px keys, every digit from the fourth on is checked against the code, so no key says how long the code is, six wrong digits clear the entry and show one wording), the saved record (only a whole record loads; a locked unit comes back locked) and the words in English and Spanish. LK_WRONG_DELAY_MS is 0: the owner chose no lockout and no pause between wrong tries for now (docs/design/lock-and-radio-2026-11-17.md records the risk); it is the one place to raise it.
